# NZ Class P — ALES Radian (or similar 2 m all-foam electric glider)
#                                                       seed definition, draft
# Rule refs: NZMAA Flying Rules, Section 5: Soaring, March 2024 (NZ.3.15,
#            plus NZ.2.4.6, NZ.2.8, NZ.1.6)
#
# Class N's shape with a 7 minute target and a 200 m limit. It is written out in
# full rather than as `like NZ-N.D` because `like` is a task-level shortcut
# within one class definition and these are two classes; that is a real cost of
# PhaseDefinition owning its tasks, and it is worth seeing.
#
# Its own contribution to the corpus is a gap rather than an extension: NZ.3.15
# makes group scoring a CD choice, and no ParameterRef slot can reach a
# Normalisation. See the foot of this file and notation §12.

class NZ-P
  name     "ALES Radian (2 m all-foam electric glider)"
  fai      ""                                                    # a national class; no FAI designation
  version  "NZMAA Section 5 Soaring, March 2024"

  param roundDuration Number s no default boundAt BeforeFlying   # NZ.3.15.1 k "decided by the CD taking into account
                                                                 #   the number of competitors, weather conditions
                                                                 #   etc. For example each round could be 1 hour" (F12)

  finalRanking SinglePhase

  reflight
    entitled     NotPermitted                                    # NZ.3.15.1 h "no re-flights are permitted"
    others       NotPermitted                                    # NZ.3.15.1 h
    minNewGroup  0                                               # no new group is ever formed

  # (no penalty definitions — every consequence in NZ.3.15 is derived from
  #  something measured)

  phase Preliminary mandatory

    rounds    FixedSequence tasksPerRound 1 maxRounds 3          # NZ.3.15 "three 7 minutes flights over 3 rounds"
    validity  minRounds 3                                        # NZ.3.15
    drop      none                                               # NZ.3.15.1 i "each flight counts"

    task D "Duration"
      metric flightTime         Number s Truncate 1              # NZ.3.15.1 f; no precision stated (F12 residual)
      metric landingDistance    Number m Truncate 0.1            # NZ.3.15.1 e; no capture precision stated
      metric motorRestarted     Flag                             # NZ.3.15.1 g
      metric airborneAtRoundEnd Flag                             # NZ.3.15.1 j — but see the note at the foot
      metric landedWithin75m    Flag                             # NZ.2.4.6

      flights   last                                             # NZ.1.6 one official flight per round
      timing    Fixed param(roundDuration) maxLaunches 1         # NZ.3.15.1 k
      group     minPerGroup 1                                    # individual scoring; see the note at the foot

      # NO `normalise` (F25). NZ.3.15.1 i: "the final score is the total of all
      # points over three flights". This is the NDC-eligible form of the class.

      flightValidWhen landedWithin75m == true                    # NZ.2.4.6

      score
        # Cumulative bands: 450 s scores 420x1 + 30x(-1) = 390.
        piecewise flightTime                                     # NZ.3.15.1 c
          0..420    @  1 pt/s                                    # NZ.3.15.1 c "one point for each second flown up to
                                                                 #   7 minutes (i.e. 420 points)"
          420..any  @ -1 pt/s                                    # NZ.3.15.1 c "then one point lost for each second
                                                                 #   flown over this time"
        when all(motorRestarted     == false,                    # NZ.3.15.1 g "landing points will be lost"
                 airborneAtRoundEnd == false)                    # NZ.3.15.1 j, read per NZ.3.13.1 j — see below
          then lookup landingDistance                            # NZ.3.15.1 e
                 <=  7 -> 50 ;  <= 15 -> 25 ;  any -> 0
          else constant 0

# ---- RULES QUERY, not a model gap ----------------------------------------
# NZ.3.15.1 j reads: "The model must be airborne at the end of the round the
# flight time for the flight & landing to count."  As written that requires a
# model to be STILL FLYING for its landing to score, which cannot be meant. The
# parallel Class N clause NZ.3.13.1 j says the opposite and makes sense: "if the
# model is still airborne at the end of the round the flight time stops at that
# point as well as no landing points awarded."
# This definition follows Class N. The reading should be confirmed with the
# NZMAA before this class is used to score a contest, and per house-keeping
# rule 1 the rule document itself is NOT to be edited to match.

# ---- unresolved for NZ Class P -------------------------------------------
# 1. GROUP SCORING IS A CD CHOICE AND IS NOT WRITABLE. NZ.3.15 preamble: "A
#    Contest Director may decide to mass launch groups of pilots to add to the
#    fun of the event. The CD may use group scoring in this instance but points
#    will not be eligible for any record claims or NDC." Whether the task
#    normalises is therefore bound at setup, and Normalisation is a value
#    object, so no ParameterRef slot reaches it (the same residual F12 hit on
#    Rounding). This file writes the individual form, which is the one that
#    counts for NDC. A group-scored Class P contest cannot currently be scored
#    by this definition. Notation §12, Left open.
# 2. The 200 m launch height and 30 s motor run are enforced by the onboard
#    altitude limiter switch (NZ.2.8) and are not scoring data.
# 3. NZ.2.8.3's launch-overrun zero is discretionary. A CD ruling.
# 4. Tie-break: NZ.3.15 states none. Finding F15.
# 5. faiDesignation is empty. Presumably nullable; nothing says so.
